      "writtenOn": "2024-12-14T07:35:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure to understand how `from_raw()` can dereference/drop the pointer before `intf.initialize()` function and effective drop of `CCallbacks`?\nI tried to implement `Drop` function, but to properly drop the `handle` I need to specify the generic parameter T:\n```\nfn drop(\u0026mut self) {                                                                            \n    unsafe { let _: Arc\u003cRwLock\u003cOption\u003cT\u003e\u003e\u003e \u003d Arc::from_raw(self.handle.cast()); }               \n}\n```\nThen I need to have the generic parameter, so `CCallbacks` becomes `CCallbacks\u003cT\u003e`, that changes `CInterface.initialize()` that should be generic now too, as It\u0027s not allowed to have generic function pointer. I need to have this generic parameter to `CInterface` too, and definitely I don\u0027t want it as a specification of the interface.\nI don\u0027t know how to manage that.",
